Note on scope: this license covers the code in src/ and dashboard/ only. The
underlying report content, figures, and findings referenced in CASE_STUDY.md
originate from "Relieving grid congestion with hydrogen" (ACT Team 3.695,
Wageningen University, 2026), co-authored by Swayam Belokar, Ilse Borsje, Jaro
van Hulst, Wytze Renema, Adebayo Salami, Lianne Schotman and Matina Vlachou.
This repository is published by one of the report's co-authors as a personal,
open-source technical extension of that group work, reproducing only the
regional (PC4-level) siting stage in Python.
